<title>FRANCE: TF1 seeks arbitration with Canal Plus.</title>
<headline>TF1 seeks arbitration with Canal Plus.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>French commercial television broadcaster TF1 said it decided to ask for arbitration by the Geneva Chambre of Commerce in its dispute with Canal Plus.</p>
<p>On Wednesday, the appeals court in Paris rejected an action by TF1 to try and block Canal Plus' merger with Nethold. TF1 argues the merger would breach a non-competition pact between TF1 and Canal Plus as joint shareholders of sports broadcaster Eurosport.</p>
<p>Nethold has a series of sports channels in various countries.</p>
<p>TF1 said in a statement that, while the Appeals Court had rejected its attempt to block the merger, the court had recognised the merger could lead to a contravention of an accord of January 8, 1993, between the two French television companies.</p>
</text>
